1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,830
This is

2
00:00:00,913 --> 00:00:07,700
an

3
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:18,750
awesome treasure

4
00:00:18,833 --> 00:00:20,137
hidden at the end of the sea,

5
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:22,857
and anyone who finds it,
the King of the Pirates!

6
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:24,397
Is that exciting or what?

7
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:28,127
There are incredible adventures
out there just waiting for us!

8
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:32,477
Bon voyage!

9
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:35,320
Have the courage that sail and believe,

10
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:39,177
and we will see a glimpse of

11
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:43,140
the sun rising on our tomorrow.

12
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:47,630
Tomorrow.

13
00:00:47,713 --> 00:00:51,940
Back when we first started,
we had separate horizons,

14
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:54,177
sailed toward different dreams.

15
00:00:54,260 --> 00:00:55,817
Things have changed now,

16
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,857
for together we found we looked
through the spyglass and see.

17
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:05,477
And we know that our hearts
have brought us here.

18
00:01:05,560 --> 00:01:09,137
Where the compass points our destiny.

19
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:13,040
There's no looking back,
take the hell with me!

20
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:17,197
Bon voyage, we can't
stop all our troubles.

21
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:19,700
Forget the past.

22
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:24,137
Though the future's
unclear, we still can smile.

23
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:26,920
We know we'll get there.

24
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:36,297
No regrets, every tear that we've
cried only helps our dreams come true.

25
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:41,497
You and those dreams
are precious in my life.

26
00:01:41,580 --> 00:01:47,260
A glimpse of the sun
rising on our tomorrow.

27
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:13,020
You listening, Pops?

28
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,680
Fatayama Brothers!

29
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,900
I did it! Huh?

30
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:18,570
Huh?

31
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:22,140
Duh, duh, duh, oh!

32
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:24,857
The City of Gold!

33
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:27,160
It was right here!

34
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,200
That bonehead!

35
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,280
He did it!

36
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:44,760
Unbelievably beautiful.

37
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:49,560
That sound is amazing! What is it?

38
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:57,280
It's come, as I always
knew it would. Destiny.

39
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:01,260
Ah, this was the ringing that Nolan heard.

40
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:03,560
Now I get it.

41
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:05,470
Yay!

42
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:06,890
Yay!

43
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:09,760
Singing.

44
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:11,250
Listen.

45
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:14,240
The Fourth is singing a song.

46
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:16,270
So...

47
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,697
This is proof.

48
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:23,220
God is real.

49
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:26,600
This is surely a miracle.

50
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:30,097
I had almost abandoned hope
that we would ever hear

51
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:34,100
the Golden Bell again after
nearly 400 years of silence.

52
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:39,240
Great warrior Kal 'gara, can you hear it?

53
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:45,220
The unmistakable echo
of the fire of Shandora.

54
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:51,280
Good heavens!

55
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:53,836
What must have happened to this land?

56
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:56,120
What is that strange chiming?

57
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:59,840
Could it be the legendary bell?

58
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,580
Mont Blanc, Noland.

59
00:04:07,980 --> 00:04:11,156
Can you hear the bell sounding
from beyond your grave?

60
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:15,988
May these chimes reverberate
all the way to your descendants.

61
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:18,640
Now rest in peace, Noland.

62
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:28,642
You like the bells ringing, too?

63
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:30,380
Yeah, I bet you do.

64
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:48,140
Old man, this is it.

65
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:52,880
Yeah, there's no doubt about it.

66
00:04:53,060 --> 00:04:56,317
Only one bell in this
world could echo so far.

67
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:58,220
And with such emotion.

68
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:04,010
Awesome.

69
00:05:04,093 --> 00:05:04,923
Absolutely.

70
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:08,612
You know those giants you see
in the cumuloregalus clouds?

71
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:11,368
The story goes a little
something like this.

72
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:15,537
Whenever a human inhabits the sky
and the sun's rays shine upon him,

73
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:19,477
his shadow is reflected on the deep
mist and then cast far across the earth.

74
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:20,390
horizon.

75
00:05:20,473 --> 00:05:25,040
To onlookers, the shadow appears as if
it's a gigantic monster looming above.

76
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:28,538
You mean those aren't really giants?

77
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:30,417
They're actually somebody's shadow?

78
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,877
That would mean we've
already found irrefutable

79
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:36,820
proof that people do live in
the sky. Am I right? Yeah.

80
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:37,960
I once thought

81
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:41,937
the story was a meaningless fantasy
and dismissed it altogether.

82
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:47,517
But it seems there is truth
to this legend my ears

83
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:50,835
are filled with the resounding
cries of the golden bell

84
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:58,517
if a golden bell exists
then why not an entire city

85
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:03,437
noland was telling the truth
his reputation can finally be

86
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:09,037
redeemed and with it our family
name that's the reason you

87
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:14,520
rang the bell isn't it Kid
shrewd move you have my thanks.

88
00:06:14,820 --> 00:06:16,560
I won't forget this

89
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:37,380
Hey, Cricket!

90
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:39,600
Are you sick? Are you hurt?

91
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:42,340
No, it's those kids.

92
00:06:42,820 --> 00:06:44,640
I'm just glad they're safe.

93
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:50,260
I was...guess I was just so worried.

94
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:10,400
Look! Up there!

95
00:07:12,360 --> 00:07:14,480
Hey, that's god shit!

96
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:20,800
Oh, thank you.

97
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:26,340
He's sunk!

98
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:31,437
God, Enru and his ship are...

99
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:32,700
falling.

100
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:42,977
The bell's ringing ignites
the fire of Shandora,

101
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:48,680
that long-gone city that took
pride above all in its prosperity.

102
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:56,720
The reverberations serve as the island's
song, proclaiming the end of the battle,

103
00:07:57,160 --> 00:08:00,477
a melody longing to be
heard by the island?

104
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:05,820
and generations of its natives
and supporters for 400 years.

105
00:08:15,140 --> 00:08:19,081
Although the journey of this restless
island seemed nearly endless,

106
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:22,580
time cannot fade even
its most distant memory.

107
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:28,060
For long ago, people entrusted their
words in the sound of the golden bell,

108
00:08:32,160 --> 00:08:35,797
lacing each ring with
words of faith and hope,

109
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:39,440
which resounded across the distant sea.

110
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,660
my friends?

111
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:50,260
it rang.

112
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:56,637
hey i wonder if pops heard it?

113
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:59,440
yeah i'm sure he did!

114
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:11,200
We're right here.

115
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:20,400
Bind the ropes to the
strongest-looking trees!

116
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:55,680
Issie, were you scared, dear?

117
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:58,700
Surprise, your treasure.

118
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:01,860
So what? Who cares?

119
00:10:03,980 --> 00:10:04,980
Lucky!

120
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:15,737
The others...

121
00:10:15,820 --> 00:10:17,860
They're fine. Don't try to speak.

122
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:21,160
Who's that over there?

123
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:23,960
Am I still alive?

124
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,795
No, you have to be treated right away.

125
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:29,226
My wounds aren't that severe.

126
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:31,990
Really.

127
00:10:32,073 --> 00:10:34,260
That guy, he needs more help than me.

128
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:35,960
Look after him.

129
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:47,160
It's true.

130
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:49,840
His body's worn out. He's dying.

131
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:52,379
Yeah, but he was trying to kill us.

132
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:54,068
We don't know him anything.

133
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:55,190
I know.

134
00:10:55,520 --> 00:11:00,108
It doesn't make much sense, but he was
going all out just like the rest of us.

135
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:03,860
He's a hero? Seriously?

136
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:06,420
Who knows?

137
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:13,540
Um, help him, raccoon doggy
I'm a reindeer antler, see?

138
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:17,520
Don't worry, you'll survive.

139
00:11:18,540 --> 00:11:19,780
Thanks, reindeer.

140
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:26,697
Yeah, you're going to overexert yourself.

141
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:28,820
Go rest with the blue sea people.

142
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:33,777
Very well, then.

143
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:36,320
I want you to go and gather the family.

144
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:41,900
I guess anything's possible.

145
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:46,377
Speaking of which, what do you think
happened to Eneru and the bell?

146
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:47,290
Don't know.

147
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:48,984
I guess they must have crashed.

148
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:53,320
So we have a city of
gold, but in name only.

149
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:57,553
Which just means that our
adventure in poverty continues.

150
00:11:58,060 --> 00:12:00,540
I'd rather have dials over gold any day.

151
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:03,577
That's something we just
can't get from the Blue Sea.

152
00:12:03,660 --> 00:12:06,897
I'm to the point where I'd
settle for some concrete news.

153
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:08,640
I hope Nami's all right.

154
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:10,060
And where's Conis?

155
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:12,536
This not-knowing is driving me crazy.

156
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:17,837
Do you think it's a good idea to leave
Wiper with the Blue Sea-Dwellers?

157
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:19,357
Don't worry, it'll be fine.

158
00:12:19,440 --> 00:12:21,357
It appears Aissa has befriended them.

159
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:23,157
We'll just have to act quickly.

160
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:25,377
If our enemy wakes before
we leave, we're finished.

161
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:27,317
Gather those who can move and we'll banish

162
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:29,917
every last one of Eneru's
priests to the clouds.

163
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:30,830
Yeah!

164
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:35,352
So did you have a chance to patch him up?

165
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:36,450
Yes.

166
00:12:36,533 --> 00:12:37,451
All he needs now is rest.

167
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:39,690
Huh?

168
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:40,870
Hey!

169
00:12:47,780 --> 00:12:48,610
Nami!

170
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:51,250
Colors!

171
00:12:51,860 --> 00:12:52,690
Luffy!

172
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:58,660
We're back!

173
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:00,820
I'm so glad you're okay!

174
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:05,587
I was afraid I wouldn't
see any of you again!

175
00:13:05,780 --> 00:13:07,240
Ah, she was worried!

176
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:09,190
Please.

177
00:13:09,273 --> 00:13:11,257
I'm glad you guys grabbed some food.

178
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:12,281
Where's it from?

179
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:16,137
We found the pre-storage locker on
our way back through the forest.

180
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:17,560
There was lots more!

181
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:20,477
But, uh, how did you manage
to find your way back down?

182
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:21,854
Well, Gum-Gum balloon!

183
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:23,210
Whoa!

184
00:13:23,293 --> 00:13:24,807
Conis, where's your old man?

185
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:28,597
Yeah, well, he...

186
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:30,237
he protected me.

187
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:32,400
and then Enoru.

188
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:38,180
Don't tell me.

189
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:43,460
I'm sorry.

190
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:45,440
Yeah, me too.

191
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,260
Me three.

192
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:51,720
You're supposed to be dead!

193
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,620
Sorry, I'm alive.

194
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:56,200
Father!

195
00:13:58,300 --> 00:14:00,857
You were on the lower
level of the White Sea?

196
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:04,234
I found myself there after
being blasted from the ledge.

197
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:06,397
And I wasn't alone.

198
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:11,057
Countless others ended up in the same spot
while making their way towards Cloud End.

199
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:16,560
Yet as we speak, they too are now on the
journey back via the restored Milky Roads.

200
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:19,797
Of course, given that there's
no longer an Angel Island,

201
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:21,586
a new destination was chosen.

202
00:14:21,980 --> 00:14:23,220
Upper Yard.

203
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:36,440
Thank you so much.

204
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:38,229
We owe you our lives, God.

205
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:39,600
Just gone, Fong.

206
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,466
I no longer go by that title.

207
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:46,400
You were all forced to work in a
place like this for six long years.

208
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:47,760
I'm sorry.

209
00:14:48,620 --> 00:14:52,208
We lost Angel Island, the home
we were supposed to return to.

210
00:14:52,460 --> 00:14:55,980
And like the Shendorians,
our birthright's now lost.

211
00:14:56,900 --> 00:14:58,700
Is the battle really over?

212
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:08,617
God's army is gone, but I just don't...

213
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:13,460
My chief, do you really believe the
400-year rift can be mended so easily?

214
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:19,060
Boy, I stuffed myself.

215
00:15:19,340 --> 00:15:20,817
Well, it's getting pretty late, you guys.

216
00:15:20,900 --> 00:15:22,429
It's time to hit the ship.

217
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,917
Whoa, you're not talking
about leaving, are you?

218
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:25,830
Relax.

219
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:28,417
Usopp, can you believe what she just said?

220
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:30,500
Hardly. It's sick. I mean,

221
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:33,337
the thought doesn't even cross her
mind to go out and look for gold,

222
00:15:33,420 --> 00:15:34,897
and she calls herself a pirate.

223
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:38,333
How do you two like fat lips
to go with your fat bellies?

224
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:48,500
It's time, and soon I will return.

225
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:52,540
To the wide open sky, the
perfect home for a god,

226
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:54,820
pristine and unobstructed.

227
00:15:56,660 --> 00:16:00,340
Yes, and best of all, no
pests to get in my way.

228
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:04,880
I'll be sure no one gets near it.

229
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:06,880
My own private paradise.

230
00:16:08,020 --> 00:16:10,380
A land boundless, exquisite.

231
00:16:11,260 --> 00:16:15,140
It's just like a dream
which comes to life.

232
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:19,970
Maxim,

233
00:16:20,053 --> 00:16:22,277
set sail and deliver me to my new floating

234
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:25,340
kingdom which shines
brightly in the night.

235
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:27,320
The land without end.

236
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:29,120
The endless birth.

237
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:36,420
Where am I?

238
00:16:37,340 --> 00:16:39,580
Inside the ruins of Shandora.

239
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:41,720
Confall.

240
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:44,180
You shouldn't move yet.

241
00:16:44,860 --> 00:16:45,690
You.

242
00:16:45,773 --> 00:16:47,020
You're a Skypeian.

243
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:51,100
Rest. Chief.

244
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:55,340
Chief, we are all bound together,
made brothers by the war.

245
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:57,480
The Golden Belfry.

246
00:16:57,640 --> 00:17:01,111
It's the Shandorian's sacred
duty to protect it to the end.

247
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,400
Listen, that's the sound of
war drums announcing battle.

248
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:09,860
There's the signal fire, too.

249
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:11,541
Patience, wiper.

250
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:13,240
Rest a while longer.

251
00:17:13,460 --> 00:17:16,000
The heroism of our ancestors is clear.

252
00:17:16,220 --> 00:17:20,760
But whatever violence happened in the
past, you must allow it to stay there.

253
00:17:21,860 --> 00:17:23,800
Our future starts here.

254
00:17:24,040 --> 00:17:27,864
This is our home now, and we
Shandians will make it a good one.

255
00:17:28,020 --> 00:17:32,220
Yes, most often the call for
vengeance cannot be ignored.

256
00:17:32,740 --> 00:17:38,600
But today, it has been drowned out by a
sea of voices screaming in celebration.

257
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:52,080
We did it!

258
00:17:53,560 --> 00:17:55,200
Yes! Yes! Yes!

259
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:07,820
All right!

260
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:15,340
All right!

261
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:17,340
All right!

262
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,940
Yes! Yes!

263
00:18:34,660 --> 00:18:58,160
Oh my god.

264
00:19:04,660 --> 00:19:09,917
I can always hear your voice
while you wander far from home.

265
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:15,237
Gazing up at the sky, you
are just like the moon.

266
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:19,820
You'll never change as
you climb into the night.

267
00:19:23,380 --> 00:19:28,800
But your reflection
waves when you disappear,

268
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:31,200
fading so silently.

269
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:37,617
Stay as you are, don't lose your way.

270
00:19:37,700 --> 00:19:40,840
Let these words guide you,

271
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:44,800
don't ever look back.

272
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:51,457
Don't give up on your dreams,
they're windless nights.

273
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:55,517
They come to you again and again.

274
00:19:55,600 --> 00:19:58,217
Until you see the journey through.

275
00:19:58,300 --> 00:20:04,097
You may not turn, I
hope that you'll learn.

276
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:09,600
To put your past behind,
and just keep moving on.
